{
  "1Kings.11.38.7-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 14 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 11:38.7</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 11:38.7</h1>\n  <h2>Change segol under vav to patah. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/14-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                       The marking under the vav is poorly written, but is clearly not a segol.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a segol, not a patah, under the vav.\n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    Ben Denckla: Breuer-DM supports replacing segol with pataḥ under vav of אצוך. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-14\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-14</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.12.25.6-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 16 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 12:25.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 12:25.6</h1>\n  <h2>Replace tipeha and patah from under resh with qamats. Poor text condition, add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/16-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                       The text is in poor condition; no tipeha is visible under the resh.\n                       This leaves the word without an accent.\n                       The blob in the second consonant could be mistaken for a dagesh; \n                          however, BHL and UXLC view it as part of a pe that was disconnected from the rest of the pe.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a qamats (not a patah) and tipeha under the resh.\n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    Ben Denckla: Breuer-DM supports the replacement of the pataḥ with qamats; \n                        however, it asserts that there is a tipeḥa under the resh.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-16\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-16</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.12.7.2-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 21 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 12:7.2</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 12:7.2</h1>\n  <h2>Replace unsupported dagesh on final vav with qubuts under resh in qere word. Add note 'q'. [וַיְדַבְּר֨וּ]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/21-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere letters, וידברו, in the right margin end in a vav, the final vav is not present in the ketiv body text letters. A qubuts mark is shown under the resh in the image. It will replace the dagesh (acting as a shuruq dot) on the final vav.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh (acting as a shuruq dot) on the final vav in the qere, וַיְדַבְּר֨וּ.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-21\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-21</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.16.33.11-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 22 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 16:33.11</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 16:33.11</h1>\n  <h2>Change hataf-segol below the aleph to a hataf-patah. \n              Remove munah below he. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/22-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    This section of text is of poor quality. \n                    No segol-like accent appears below the aleph.\n                    No munah is apparent below the he.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a hataf-segol on the aleph and a tsere followed by munah on the he.\n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-22\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-22</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.16.33.13-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 23 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 16:33.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 16:33.13</h1>\n  <h2>Remove qadma above the kaf. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/23-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>This section of text is of poor quality. \n                       Two words are shown in the image; the first word is word 13, the subject of this change.\n                       The dagesh and the holam on the kaf are very faint.\n                       Comparing the lameds in both words shows no evidence of an accent on the final lamed of word 13.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a holam and a dagesh on the kaf. It also has a pashta on the lamed.\n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-23\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-23</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.17.13.11-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 24 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 17:13.11</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 17:13.11</h1>\n  <h2>Replace munah under lamed with meteg. Add maqaf to end of word. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/24-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>This section of text is of poor quality. \n                 Note the verse has two words of lamed followed by yod; this word is the first lamed followed by yod.\n                 No munah is apparent on the lamed, the hiriq and meteg are very faint.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a hiriq followed by munah under the lamed. It has no maqaf at the end of the word.\n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word; it does have an entry for word 16 in this verse, however. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-24\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-24</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.17.15.8-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.01.14, number: 3 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 17:15.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 17:15.8</h1>\n  <h2>Remove meteg under he. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2024.01.14/3-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The image is the LC body text which consists of the ketiv consonants, הוא־והיא (2 words), with the qere pointing. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  The first qere consonants, היא appear the right of the column, \n\t\t\t\t\t\t     the second qere consonants, והוא , appear to the left of the column.  \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  Words 6, 7, 8, 9 of the UXLC represent both the LC body text and the qere consonants; \n\t\t\t\t\t\t     words 6, 7 contain the ketiv variants for this image; \n\t\t\t\t\t\t         UXLC word 8 is the first qere word, shown in the Reference/Change above.  \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  This change is to the UXLC word 8, a qere word. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  No meteg is apparent under the he, only a hiriq. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  The evidence for a maqaf between the alef and the second vav is weak. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  A note 't' will be added to this first qere word; \n\t\t\t\t\t\t      this note about the maqaf also applies to the UXLC ketiv word 6.\n\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n  <p>BHL agrees with this change in both the qere and ketiv.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2024.01.14-3\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2024.01.14-3</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.17.23.13-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 26 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 17:23.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 17:23.13</h1>\n  <h2>Remove tipeha under aleph.  Add note 't'</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/26-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                       The text quality is very poor here. \n                       The top, left side of the lamed on the following line might be taken as an accent on the aleph or yod. \n                       No tipeha under the aleph is apparent.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a sheva under the resh and a hiriq and tipeha under the aleph. \n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word. \n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-26\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-26</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.2.13.4-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.12.07 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.08.31, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 2:13.4</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 2:13.4</h1>\n  <h2>Damaged text. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/images/2022.08.31/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The text is damaged, particularly on the gimel and yod.</p>\n  <p>\n                    The BHL has a dagesh, hireq, and revia on the gimel.\n                    BHL Appendix A has no entry for this word, word 4; it does have an entry for words 6, 7, however.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes/2022.12.07 - Changes.xml?2022.08.31-2\">2022.12.07 - Changes.xml : 2022.08.31-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "1Kings.7.45.11-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 19 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Kings_1 7:45.11</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Kings_1 7:45.11</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from lamed in qere word. Add note 'q'. [הָאֵ֔לֶּה]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/19-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere letters, האלה, in the right margin have the order of the lamed and final he reversed relative to those, האהל, of the ketiv body text. Most of the markings on the ketiv body text are easily applied to the qere letters. The body text does not support a dagesh in the lamed, however. This action may be explained in Dotan's BHL page xx for Deut 28:27.6: The ketiv he can not take a dagesh, thus the writer didn't place a dagesh there. Nevertheless, no dagesh appears in the LC to justify a dagesh in the lamed. Add note 'q'.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the lamed of the qere, הָאֵ֔לֶּה. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-19\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-19</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
